{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977781591,"sessionID":"ses_1ccaa8a51ffe66fcrNKIYLeG3y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_oWCS7dAkBCh4K9vigETwXZaA","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Updated `CL_0001041` so CXCR3 is modeled with `has plasma membrane part` (`RO_0002104`) instead of `has part`, matching the receptor-localization pattern already used for related CXCR3-positive/negative T-cell terms.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Updated `CL_0001041` (`CD8-positive, CXCR3-positive, alpha-beta regulatory T cell`) in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` to use `has plasma membrane part` (`RO_0002104`) for CXCR3 (`PR_000001207`) in its equivalence axiom.\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue requested replacing `has part` with `has plasma membrane part` for CXCR3 because CXCR3 is a plasma membrane receptor.\n+- This aligns `CL_0001041` with the documented CL pattern for receptor-positive cell types in `docs/patterns/cellHasPlasmaMembranePartX.md`.\n+- It also makes this term consistent with related CXCR3-modeled T-cell classes that already use `RO_0002104` for positive receptor expression and `lacks_plasma_membrane_part` for negative expression.\n+\n+Checklist completed:\n+- Read the imported issue context from `__issue_context__.json`.\n+- Checked the CL plasma membrane part pattern documentation.\n+- Inspected the existing `CL_0001041` axiom and nearby CXCR3-related modeling examples.\n+- Made the minimal ontology edit in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Reviewed the git diff to confirm only the intended relation changed for this term.\n+- Committed only `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` locally.\n+\n+Validation performed:\n+- Pattern review against `docs/patterns/cellHasPlasmaMembranePartX.md`.\n+- Diff review confirming the equivalence axiom changed from `BFO_0000051` to `RO_0002104` for `PR_000001207` and no other ontology content was intentionally modified.\n+\n+Local commit:\n+- `7d22653` - `Use has plasma membrane part for CL_0001041 CXCR3`\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Updated `CL_0001041` so CXCR3 is modeled with `has plasma membrane part` (`RO_0002104`) instead of `has part`, matching the receptor-localization pattern already used for related CXCR3-positive/negative T-cell terms.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@\n+Updated `CL_0001041` (`CD8-positive, CXCR3-positive, alpha-beta regulatory T cell`) in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` to use `has plasma membrane part` (`RO_0002104`) for CXCR3 (`PR_000001207`) in its equivalence axiom.\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue requested replacing `has part` with `has plasma membrane part` for CXCR3 because CXCR3 is a plasma membrane receptor.\n+- This aligns `CL_0001041` with the documented CL pattern for receptor-positive cell types in `docs/patterns/cellHasPlasmaMembranePartX.md`.\n+- It also makes this term consistent with related CXCR3-modeled T-cell classes that already use `RO_0002104` for positive receptor expression and `lacks_plasma_membrane_part` for negative expression.\n+\n+Checklist completed:\n+- Read the imported issue context from `__issue_context__.json`.\n+- Checked the CL plasma membrane part pattern documentation.\n+- Inspected the existing `CL_0001041` axiom and 